       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum ibuprofen dose of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and there's no added benefit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day). This is a typical analgesic dose.\n\nDid you mean 1600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily? Or is there a different dose you intended? Once you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note on the order. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
